# Refurbished Linux - the desktop itself.
# labwc is the compositor; refurb-shell (shipped as a .deb in
# config/packages.chroot) draws the bar, launcher and windows.
labwc
# Established front ends for the jobs the shell should not reimplement.
# Each one is a normal application: no daemon, nothing resident until its
# window is open, and it talks to the same NetworkManager/BlueZ/PipeWire the
# custom controls already use.
#   nm-connection-editor
#                  Wi-Fi: NetworkManager's own editor - scan, security, saved
#                  networks, autoconnect. The quick panel's dialog stays as the
#                  shortcut. (iwgtk is iwd-only in Debian and shows "iwd is
#                  down" on this image, which runs NetworkManager.)
#   blueman        Bluetooth: BlueZ's manager - discovery, pairing agents,
#                  trusted devices and audio profiles.
#   pavucontrol    PipeWire's mixer: per-application streams, input devices,
#                  and headset profiles.
#   mako-notifier  The org.freedesktop.Notifications service, so failures from
#                  those programs are actually shown. Wayland-native, ~2 MB.
nm-connection-editor
blueman
pavucontrol
mako-notifier
# Seat management without a display manager or a logind graphical session:
# libseat's seatd backend hands the compositor DRM and VT access directly.
# About 1 MB resident, and it replaces a display manager entirely.
seatd
xwayland
foot
pcmanfm
gvfs
xdg-utils
swaylock
wlr-randr
grim
# On-screen display for the volume/brightness keys (about 40 KB).
wob
brightnessctl
xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
desktop-file-utils
shared-mime-info
xdg-user-dirs
udisks2
upower
fonts-inter
fonts-dejavu-core
libgl1-mesa-dri
mesa-va-drivers
intel-media-va-driver
gnome-themes-extra
adwaita-icon-theme
